<title>ITALY: Bank of Italy selling up to 1.5 trln lire BOTs.</title>
<headline>Bank of Italy selling up to 1.5 trln lire BOTs.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Italy said it was offering to sell up to 1.5 trillion lire of short term bills (BOT).</p>
<p>Bids must be received by 0800 GMT today.</p>
<p>The sale offer is for January 15, January 31 and February 14, 1997 bills.</p>
<p>At its previous sale on Tuesday of a similar amount of BOTs to drain liquidity from the money market, the maximum rate was 7.95 percent and average rate 7.91 percent.</p>
</text>
